WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.800
Welcome to Orders Shop, the web front
end for the Orders API.

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:09.128
This tour uses the real app, running
locally with demo data.

00:00:09.128 --> 00:00:13.528
We start as a customer, and then
switch to the administrator.

00:00:15.297 --> 00:00:17.097
This is the sign-in page.

00:00:17.097 --> 00:00:20.121
A new customer starts with Create account.

00:00:20.829 --> 00:00:25.181
Registration asks for a name, an
email, and a password.

00:00:25.181 --> 00:00:31.749
If the password is too short, the form says so
right away, before anything is sent.

00:00:32.458 --> 00:00:37.689
The password needs at least fifteen
characters, with no composition rules,

00:00:37.689 --> 00:00:39.315
and spaces are allowed.

00:00:39.315 --> 00:00:41.506
So a short sentence works well.

00:00:42.219 --> 00:00:45.906
The result is always the same
check your email message,

00:00:45.906 --> 00:00:49.257
whether or not the address was
already registered.

00:00:49.257 --> 00:00:51.603
That keeps account lookups private.

00:00:52.309 --> 00:00:56.661
If you try to sign in before
confirming, the app explains why,

00:00:56.661 --> 00:00:59.749
and offers to resend the
confirmation email.

00:01:00.462 --> 00:01:03.296
In this local setup, email is simulated,

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:07.193
and the confirmation link is
written to the server log.

00:01:07.193 --> 00:01:09.461
Opening it confirms the address,

00:01:09.461 --> 00:01:13.854
and the app removes the token from the
address bar right away.

00:01:14.567 --> 00:01:16.679
Now the customer can sign in.

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:24.684
Signed-in customers land on the
catalog: eight demo products,

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:27.436
each with a price and a stock state.

00:01:28.147 --> 00:01:32.637
Search matches name or SKU, and
starts after two characters.

00:01:32.637 --> 00:01:34.808
One letter only shows a hint.

00:01:34.808 --> 00:01:39.822
Typing key narrows the list, and the
search is kept in the address,

00:01:39.822 --> 00:01:42.067
so the page can be bookmarked.

00:01:42.768 --> 00:01:44.841
Sorting and filters work too.

00:01:44.841 --> 00:01:48.273
Here the list runs from most to
least expensive,

00:01:48.273 --> 00:01:52.920
limited to products under one hundred
dollars, and in stock only.

00:01:53.631 --> 00:01:56.838
Opening a product shows its
details and stock,

00:01:56.838 --> 00:02:00.255
with a quantity picker and an
add to cart button.

00:02:00.967 --> 00:02:05.298
Let's add the keyboard, and then a
wireless mouse from the list.

00:02:05.298 --> 00:02:08.479
The cart count in the header
updates each time.

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:13.455
In the cart, quantities can be
changed and products removed,

00:02:13.455 --> 00:02:15.730
and the estimated total follows.

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:20.350
The cart lives in this browser, and is
cleared when you sign out.

00:02:21.053 --> 00:02:26.460
Placing the order checks current prices and
stock, and sends it just once.

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:31.209
The new order opens right away as
pending, with its items, total,

00:02:31.209 --> 00:02:32.597
and status history.

00:02:33.309 --> 00:02:39.001
My orders lists every order, with filters for
status and dates, and sorting.

00:02:39.001 --> 00:02:41.997
The filters stay in the address as well.

00:02:42.698 --> 00:02:46.685
A pending order can be cancelled,
with an optional reason.

00:02:46.685 --> 00:02:50.810
The status changes to cancelled, and
the history records it.

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:53.804
My account shows the profile.

00:02:53.804 --> 00:02:55.615
The email is read only.

00:02:55.615 --> 00:02:59.632
Edit profile changes the name
and the phone number.

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:03.890
Changing the password signs you
out on every device,

00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:06.484
so you sign in again with the new one.

00:03:11.954 --> 00:03:16.514
Sign out everywhere ends the sessions
on all devices at once.

00:03:17.226 --> 00:03:22.906
If you forget the password, enter the email and
you always see the same message.

00:03:22.906 --> 00:03:28.658
The reset link, again from the server log,
opens a page to choose a new password,

00:03:28.658 --> 00:03:30.930
and then returns you to sign-in.

00:03:31.635 --> 00:03:34.351
Customers cannot open the back office.

00:03:34.351 --> 00:03:37.995
The admin address shows a
not-allowed page instead.

00:03:38.709 --> 00:03:41.300
Delete account explains what happens.

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:45.852
Personal details are erased, order
records are kept without them,

00:03:45.852 --> 00:03:47.883
and you cannot sign in again.

00:03:47.883 --> 00:03:51.525
It asks for the current password
and a confirmation.

00:03:52.227 --> 00:03:55.971
Afterwards, the same
credentials no longer work.

00:03:59.267 --> 00:04:04.258
Administrators sign in on the same page,
and land in the back office.

00:04:04.258 --> 00:04:09.683
The dashboard shows the low-stock count, and
the last thirty days of sales.

00:04:10.392 --> 00:04:16.128
The Products section lists every product,
with search, sorting, and paging.

00:04:16.842 --> 00:04:20.508
Creating a product validates
the form first.

00:04:20.508 --> 00:04:25.506
Then the name, SKU, description,
price, and stock are saved.

00:04:26.534 --> 00:04:31.361
Editing loads the latest version and
saves with a concurrency check,

00:04:31.361 --> 00:04:34.981
so two admins cannot silently
overwrite each other.

00:04:34.981 --> 00:04:36.614
Here I raise the stock.

00:04:37.318 --> 00:04:39.574
Deleting asks for confirmation.

00:04:39.574 --> 00:04:43.577
It is a soft delete: customers
stop seeing the product,

00:04:43.577 --> 00:04:46.270
and existing orders keep their lines.

00:04:46.985 --> 00:04:51.161
With Include deleted ticked, the
product shows as deleted,

00:04:51.161 --> 00:04:53.033
and one click restores it.

00:04:55.048 --> 00:04:59.867
That is the customer portal, and the
first part of the back office.

00:04:59.867 --> 00:05:03.175
Screens for customers, orders,
reports, users,

00:05:03.175 --> 00:05:06.340
and audit logs are not in the
interface yet.

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:09.504
For now those are available
through the API.

00:05:09.504 --> 00:05:15.186
To try it yourself, start the stack with
docker compose up, and open localhost,

00:05:15.186 --> 00:05:17.056
port eight zero eight one.
